The micro-qwen3 model follows the Qwen3 architecture; it is trained from scratch
and contains no Qwen weights.

The model was trained on TinyStories and TinyStoriesInstruct by Ronen Eldan and Yuanzhi Li (2023), released
under the Community Data License Agreement, Sharing, Version 1.0 (CDLA-Sharing-1.0).
web/corpus-4grams.bin holds counts of four-token phrases from TinyStories V2; as data derived from that
dataset it is shared under the same CDLA-Sharing-1.0 license (https://cdla.dev/sharing-1-0/).

